From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:02:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple-h9p: Don't detach power domains that were never
 attached

apple_h9p_pcie_attach_genpd() only allocates pd_dev and pd_link when the
node lists more than one power domain; with a single domain the driver
core attaches it and both arrays stay NULL. The cleanup action is
registered either way, so on a probe failure or unbind of a controller
with exactly one power domain, apple_h9p_pcie_detach_genpd() walks
pd_count entries of NULL arrays and dereferences pd_link[0].

Return early when the arrays were never allocated. This affects every
controller described with one power domain: T8010 (ps_pcie) today, and
the T8015 controller added next.

[Orchard: split out of the T8015 support patch, message written in review]
Signed-off-by: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
index e522379..39eb0f7 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
@@ -907,6 +907,9 @@ static void apple_h9p_pcie_detach_genpd(struct apple_h9p_pcie *pcie)
 {
 	int i;
 
+	if (!pcie->pd_dev || !pcie->pd_link)
+		return;
+
 	for (i = pcie->pd_count - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
 		if (pcie->pd_link[i])
 			device_link_del(pcie->pd_link[i]);
